mirror against preview02, 720p, CRF 26. Residual after a 9-row running mean, luma 0..255.
r = mirror vs frame on the same rows. off1 = one row off. wrong = the plate's top moved 1.3 px, a wrong lattice
seam r takes the seam-free mirror (aa 0 + guard) away from both first, so what is left is the seams alone. It matters
on sin z, whose real horizontal bands dominate r and leave off1 and wrong high.
